## Context

This decision supersedes [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject).
The accepted historical record is unchanged. The reports merged into
[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) contain both a shared-parser failure and a booking-v3
hint failure. Similar subjects hid different causes, while different subjects described
the same cause. Intake tags also disagree with tenant and form evidence.

## Decision

Use the tenant directory and report channel with the existing `causeOf` and `sameCause`
functions. The tenant locale, not the reporter's browser locale, determines date order.
For day-first tenants, form reports on booking-v3 belong to the hint cause; other
channels and booking-v2 belong to the parser cause. Count unique report IDs, not export rows.

Merge only when both reports have the same known cause. Unknown tenants and reports
without an established cause stay apart pending investigation, even if subjects match.
Read the body and retain conflicting symptoms as evidence; a tenant-derived classification
is not proof that every reported symptom has the same mechanism.

## Check the rule

<DedupeExplorer />

## Consequences

The desk keeps one engineering ticket per known cause, with an auditable report count.
Triage requires a tenant lookup, rather than a subject-only shortcut. Missing metadata
requires review rather than an automatic merge. Recompute the incident's live tables and
render the page after data changes; do not copy old counts into standing guidance.

